---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageMeta from '@/components/PageMeta.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Source material and SharePoint"
  description="How working-group members submit authorised evidence through isolated SharePoint organisation folders."
>
  <PageMeta category="Working groups · Member guide" variant="brand" updated="Evidence guidance · 21 August 2026" />
  <h1>Source material and SharePoint</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Evidence intake is separate from group discussion. An active group uses a separate
    SharePoint source-intake site with one private organisation folder per approved
    company domain; the Team-connected Shared Documents library is not the controlled
    intake boundary.
  </p>

  <h2 id="access">How the intake area works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The Team roster identifies approved participants.</li>
    <li>An approved company-domain account may be placed in its organisation's contributor group.</li>
    <li>The participant can browse the intake index and open only the organisation folder they are permitted to use.</li>
    <li>Other participating organisations cannot view that folder or its contents.</li>
    <li>Contributors may organise their own folder, but cannot change permissions or make material public.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    A generic-provider account may take part in Teams but does not receive a provider-wide
    SharePoint folder. Ask OPDA to add an authorised company-domain contributor instead.
  </p>

  <h2 id="readme">Make every submission understandable</h2>
  <p>Maintain a README at the top of the organisation area containing:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>an index of submitted files and folders;</li>
    <li>the source organisation, owner or steward;</li>
    <li>version, date and the period for which the material applies;</li>
    <li>the relevant working-group context and what the material demonstrates;</li>
    <li>whether it is authoritative, informative, illustrative or disputed; and</li>
    <li>licence, confidentiality, retention, reuse and interpretation restrictions.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="useful-material">Useful material</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Examples</th><th>What it can show</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Standards and interfaces</td><td>JSON Schema, OpenAPI, AsyncAPI, GraphQL and XML Schema</td><td>Existing exchange requirements and implementation constraints.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Data structures</td><td>Data dictionaries, field lists, ER diagrams and non-production DDL</td><td>Terms, cardinalities, identifiers and dependencies.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Business material</td><td>Policies, guidance, blank forms, contracts and handbooks</td><td>Definitions, rules, obligations and exceptions.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Semantic material</td><td>RDF, OWL, SKOS, SHACL, JSON-LD and mappings</td><td>Reuse candidates, vocabularies, validation and lineage.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Examples</td><td>Anonymised scenarios, valid/invalid samples, diagrams and screenshots</td><td>Competency questions, edge cases and test expectations.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Meeting evidence</td><td>Authorised transcripts with date, speakers and context</td><td>Rationale, disagreement, corrections and open questions.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2 id="do-not-submit">Do not submit</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Personal, customer or live property-transaction data.</li>
    <li>Passwords, API keys, credentials, private keys, connection details or other secrets.</li>
    <li>Material restricted by confidentiality, contract, licence or NDA.</li>
    <li>Executables, active scripts, macros, encrypted files, password-protected files or archives.</li>
    <li>Links to websites, cloud drives, shared folders or online documents in place of the source file.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Audio and video files are not accepted through the current intake. Supply a
    permitted transcript with its date, speakers and context. Upload only material your
    organisation is authorised to share with OPDA for this work.
  </p>

  <h2 id="what-happens">What happens after submission</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>OPDA preserves the original and screens file type, rights, sensitivity and suitability.</li>
    <li>Approved information is registered with provenance and the relevant context.</li>
    <li>Facilitators may use it to frame questions or model candidates.</li>
    <li>People review any proposition before it advances beyond candidate status.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    A submission is not automatically public and is not automatically shared with other
    participants. If SharePoint is blocked, email fallback is available only when the sender's
    organisation resolves from an approved company-domain identity and live SharePoint
    membership. Permitted, allowlisted attachments of at most 50 MiB may be accepted at
    <a href="mailto:smartdata@openpropdata.org.uk">smartdata@openpropdata.org.uk</a>. Larger or
    unknown files require manual review; links are not followed, and the same screening and
    isolated organisation boundary still apply.
  </p>
</Layout>
